{"ts":"2026-07-27T01:53:33.846Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_instance":"983770245168f533a68a42dd","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-mkzw1x"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Merge-fence scope ambiguity: extension-contributed item folders make default validation disagree with the no-extensions CI baseline"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Default extension-aware pm validate and pm merge install include item types contributed by active project extensions, while the repository merge-safety CI deliberately runs both commands with --no-extensions. The same committed .gitattributes can therefore be reported stale locally and over-specified in CI. Define a stable project-schema versus optional-runtime-extension fence contract, surface the selected scope in diagnostics, and ensure one documented command produces the committed baseline without contradictory remediation."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["ci","extensions","merge","multi-agent","ux","validation"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-27T01:53:33.846Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-27T01:53:33.846Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The committed fence has one explicit reproducible schema scope shared by CI and operator guidance; default validation does not recommend a change that the required CI gate reverses; diagnostics name whether core project schema or active extension schema was audited; tests cover tracked project profiles and optional runtime-only profiles without weakening custom item merge protection"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-g5sx"},{"op":"add","p